    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Isaac Paredes** emerges as our premier option, boasting a 70.39 efficiency score that easily clears the field. His projection is bolstered by a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez and an assumed premium spot in the order, which allows him to maximize volume against a moderate-skill arm. Behind him, **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte** offer high-upside stability; both benefit significantly from batting at the top of the lineup against a middling pitcher like Dobnak. While **Jose Caballero** remains a high-risk, high-reward play due to his elite stolen base potential, his efficiency is currently depressed by a bottom-of-the-order assignment, reinforcing our strategy to lean on guys like **Paredes** for safer production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who registered a 50.99 score but ultimately fell short of the starting criteria. While he provides a reliable floor, his dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Jump tipped the scales in favor of our active infielders, who carry more favorable handedness matchups. We are closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Isaac Paredes** and **Jose Caballero**; should either shift down significantly in their respective batting orders, we may need to pivot. Furthermore, while we aren't starting him today, we continue to monitor the long-term status of **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom** on the IL, as their return will be vital for re-evaluating our offensive depth alongside mainstays like **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Austin Riley**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo**.",
